    80	\begin{abstract}
    81	A pair of orthogonal latin cubes of order $q$ is equivalent to an
    82	MDS code with distance $3$ or to an ${\rm OA}_1(3,5,q)$  orthogonal
    83	array. We construct pairs of orthogonal latin cubes for a sequence
    84	of previously unknown orders $q_i=16(18i-1)+4$ and
    85	$q'_i=16(18i+5)+4$. The minimal new obtained parameters of
    86	orthogonal arrays are ${\rm OA}_1(3,5,84)$.
    87	
    88	\textit{Keywords}--- latin square, latin cube, MOLS, MDS code, block
    89	design, Steiner system, orthogonal array
    90	
    91	\end{abstract}
    92	
    93	MSC2010: 05B15, 94B05,  05B05
    94	
