The native alternatives do not survive the same test. A codeword-completion variant is solved by constant-size linear algebra when the paper’s compressed linear representation is shown; hiding that representation turns it into an unrelated reconstruction puzzle. A symbolic “construction recipe” is short, but for Theorem 2 it is merely the displayed formula \(q=16(6s\pm1)+4\), so there is no nontrivial answer search. The honest native witness remains the full OA/MDS code, whose size is already fatal before hardness tuning. I’m checking the repository’s rejection schema and will record the exact lower bounds rather than manufacture a convenience problem.
