Rejected at Step 0. The paper’s Theorem 2 is an explicit construction, so G and V are achievable, but H fails on both tracks.

At the first new order \(q=84\), a cube-pair witness requires 1,185,408 symbols—far beyond the 256-atom cap. A symbolic theorem invocation is writable but reduces to direct substitution in \(q=16(6s\pm1)+4\), leaving no meaningful search. The paper provides no hardness result for planted completion or reconstruction variants. These conclusions follow from Propositions 1, 3, 6 and Theorems 1–3 in the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1911.12960).

The complete audit, including mechanical-versus-compact costs and rejected alternatives, is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1911.12960/REJECTED.md). Per the Step-0 stopping rule, no generator or oracle evidence was fabricated.
